{
  "machineFile": "submachine.fsm",
  "description": "Submachine runtime semantics (Doc 08 §12). Device's root-initial lands on `Connecting`, a `state Connecting is Connection` submachine reference, so a nested Connection sub-instance is instantiated + initialised at the template's initial state Idle (§12.2, no named entry-point → implicit initial). CONNECT / ACK / ESTABLISHED are not consumed by the parent (Connecting only handles RECONNECT and the `done` completion) so each delegates into the sub-instance's RTC (§12.1, after the established transition-wins parent selection): the sub runs Idle -> Handshake -> Established -> Done(final). Reaching the sub's `final` (§12.3) makes the parent receive a synthetic completion, which fires `Connecting --done--> Online` through the EXISTING completion machinery (note `eventReceived.name = __completion__:s-Device-Connecting`, the same R1 done-autofire path every other completion uses — not duplicated) with NO external event, and exiting Connecting tears the sub-instance down (`exitedStates: [s-Device-Connecting]`). The interleaved `submachine_event_delegated` / nested `dispatched` / `submachine_completed` records are the byte-deterministic sub-instance trace W2d reuses for gcc sim≡codegen matching.",
  "init": {
    "machineName": "Device"
  },
